+### PNG Parameter Compression (8-bit)
+**Definition:** Compresses neural network parameters into a single 8-bit PNG image using min-max normalization and integer quantization [S2, unofficial].
+**Step:** Reshape parameters to a grid, compute global min/max, normalize to $[0,1]$, scale to $[0, 255]$, round to uint8, save as PNG, and store shape, dtype, mins, and maxs in metadata [S2, unofficial].
+**Formula:** $img = \lfloor \frac{grid - mins}{maxs - mins} \times 255 \rceil$ [S2, unofficial].
+**Code:** `img = (img_norm * (2**8 - 1)).round().astype(np.uint8)` [S2, unofficial].
+
 ## Background
-The method originates from research into compressing Instant-NGP-based NeRFs, specifically addressing the memory overhead of hash grids and MLPs in neural rendering [S1]. The development highlights the trade-off between compression ratio and rendering quality, demonstrating that differentiable quantization during training can mitigate the accuracy loss typically seen in post-training quantization [S1]. It is used in contexts requiring efficient storage and transmission of neural volume data, such as real-time rendering on constrained hardware or large-scale scene archiving [S1].
+The method originates from research on compressing Instant-NGP-based NeRFs, specifically addressing the memory overhead of hash grids and MLPs in neural rendering [S1]. It is also applied to scientific volume data using Implicit Neural Representations (INRs) to serve as both compressed storage and a queryable data source [S2, unofficial].
 
